  { image: img('hiking/gallery_08.jpg'), alt: 'Bromeliads growing on a trailside tree' },
  { image: img('hiking/gallery_21.jpg'), alt: 'A mossy tree trunk beside the trail', size: 'tall' },
  { image: img('hiking/gallery_22.jpg'), alt: 'The trail winding deeper into the cloud forest', size: 'lg' },
  { image: img('hiking/gallery_13.jpg'), alt: 'Moss and epiphytes on a trailside branch' },
  { image: img('hiking/gallery_23.jpg'), alt: 'A hiker facing a waterfall deep in the cloud forest', size: 'tall' },
  { image: img('hiking/gallery_48.jpg'), alt: 'A family laughing on the way down, the youngest in a carrier', size: 'tall' },
  { image: img('hiking/gallery_20.jpg'), alt: 'The trail disappearing into mist' },
  { image: img('hiking/gallery_30.jpg'), alt: 'Ruffled orange bracket fungus growing on a mossy log', size: 'tall' },
  { image: img('hiking/gallery_25.jpg'), alt: 'Hikers pausing at a lookout over the forested ridges', size: 'wide' },
  { image: img('hiking/gallery_38.jpg'), alt: 'A hiker pushing up through dense, wet undergrowth' },
  { image: img('hiking/gallery_27.jpg'), alt: 'Hikers among tall trees and hanging vines on the trail', size: 'tall' },
  { image: img('hiking/gallery_42.jpg'), alt: 'A hiker clambering over a mossy fallen log' },
  { image: img('hiking/gallery_10.jpg'), alt: 'Tree roots crossing the trail' },
  { image: img('hiking/gallery_33.jpg'), alt: 'A deep pink flower blooming in the cloud forest understory', size: 'tall' },
  { image: img('hiking/gallery_29.jpg'), alt: 'A hiker scrambling up a muddy, root-laced section of the trail' },
  { image: img('hiking/gallery_31.jpg'), alt: 'A hiker with a red backpack pushing through ferns and hanging moss' },
  { image: img('hiking/gallery_28.jpg'), alt: 'Hikers climbing a steep trail under moss-draped cloud forest trees', size: 'tall' },
  { image: img('hiking/gallery_45.jpg'), alt: 'Arms raised toward the cloud forest canopy' },
  { image: img('hiking/gallery_52.jpg'), alt: 'A family among the tree ferns, a toddler riding in a carrier' },
  { image: img('hiking/gallery_35.jpg'), alt: 'Clusters of white wild mushrooms in the grass beside the trail', size: 'wide' },
  { image: img('hiking/gallery_34.jpg'), alt: 'A hiker crawling under a fallen tree across the trail', size: 'tall' },
];
---

<PageLayout
  title="Hiking the Cloud Forest | Wild on the Farm, Boquete Cloud Forest Lodge"
  description="Trails into Amistad National Park, starting at the farm's doorstep — moss-draped cloud forest, monkeys, and views over the Chiriquí highlands."
  path="/hiking/"
  image={ogImage.src}
  pullIntro="Hiking Boquete cloud forest, far from the crowds. No shuttle, no trailhead parking lot — just a gate, and then moss, mist, and the sound of the forest waking up."
>
  <Fragment slot="hero">
    <PhotoHero image={heroImage} alt="Hiking the cloud forest at Wild on the Farm" eyebrow="Hiking Amistad National Park — Far From The Crowds">
      Trails that start at our door and end inside the clouds.
    </PhotoHero>
  </Fragment>

  <Section label="On the Trail" heading="What you'll walk through.">
    <Split>
      <div>
        <p>
          The trails climb through primary cloud forest — moss-wrapped trunks, bromeliads, tree
          ferns — with the kind of quiet that makes every distant call or rustle in the canopy
          impossible to ignore. White-faced capuchins and mantled howler monkeys move through the
          same territory, often spotted straight overhead.
        </p>
      </div>
      <div>
        <div class="amenity-list">
          {amenities.map((item) => <span>{item}</span>)}
        </div>
      </div>
    </Split>
    <p><a href="/journal/hiking-in-boquete/"><strong>The trails of Boquete, their history, and our own map →</strong></a></p>
  </Section>

  <Section label="For Experienced Hikers" heading="Amistad Wild Crossing.">
    <Split>
      <div>
        <p>
          Our most demanding crossing: a hike through mountain and jungle terrain, about 11 kilometres from the Pianista valley to Wild on the Farm, through a wild, mountainous part of La Amistad National Park. The trail is sensed more than followed — fallen trees to climb over, rivers to cross, 850 metres of elevation gain.
        </p>
        <p>
          The forest is beautiful and keeps changing mood, right up to the windswept ridges at the end. This is the territory of the tapir, the peccary, monkeys, deer, the ocelot, the puma and the jaguar — and of the quetzal.
        </p>
        <p>
          <strong>Bring:</strong> very good hiking shoes or boots, a fleece, rain gear and a windbreaker, a small light backpack and at least one litre of water. The gourmet picnic is included.
        </p>
      </div>
      <div>
        <div class="amenity-list">
          {amistadFacts.map((item) => <span>{item}</span>)}
        </div>
      </div>
    </Split>
    <NoteBox>
      <p>
        The route is unmarked and can only be walked with a guide, in groups of 6 at most. The return to Boquete is by car from Wild on the Farm.
      </p>
      <p>
        A liability waiver is signed before departure: every participant must have insurance that covers them in case of a hiking accident.
      </p>
    </NoteBox>
    <a class="btn btn-normal btn-spaced" href={`?randonnee=${amistadWildCrossing.slug}#reserver`}>Book this trail</a>
    {amistadMaps.map((map) => (
      <div class="wide-photo">
        <Image src={map.image} alt={map.alt} widths={[480, 900, 1600, 2000]} sizes="100vw" />
      </div>
    ))}
  </Section>

  <Section label="Moderate" heading="Cloud Forest and Waterfall.">
    <Split>
      <div>
        <p>
          A 6.5-kilometre loop through mountain terrain, starting from the Camino del Español: the cloud forest, the waterfall, and beautiful ridges. The slopes are steep, with 400 metres of elevation gain up to 1,918 metres.
        </p>
        <p>
          <strong>Bring:</strong> very good hiking shoes or boots, a fleece, rain gear and a windbreaker, a small light backpack and at least one litre of water. The gourmet picnic is included.
        </p>
      </div>
      <div>
        <div class="amenity-list">
          {waterfallFacts.map((item) => <span>{item}</span>)}
        </div>
      </div>
    </Split>
    <a class="btn btn-normal btn-spaced" href={`?randonnee=${cloudForestWaterfall.slug}#reserver`}>Book this trail</a>
    {waterfallMaps.map((map) => (
      <div class="wide-photo">
        <Image src={map.image} alt={map.alt} widths={[480, 900, 1600, 2000]} sizes="100vw" />
      </div>
    ))}
  </Section>

  <Section label="For All Hikers" heading="Farm Tour and Cloud Forest.">
    <Split>
      <div>
        <p>
          A loop of about 4 hours from the bottom of the farm: up into the cloud forest, a beautiful forest, then a discovery of Wild on the Farm. The slopes are steep: 200 metres of elevation gain, from 1,700 to 1,918 metres.
        </p>
        <p>
          At the farm: the macadamia plantation, the animals, and an introduction to permaculture. A meal can be added for an extra charge.
        </p>
      </div>
      <div>
        <div class="amenity-list">
          {farmTourFacts.map((item) => <span>{item}</span>)}
        </div>
      </div>
    </Split>
    <a class="btn btn-normal btn-spaced" href={`?randonnee=${farmTourCloudForest.slug}#reserver`}>Book this trail</a>
    {farmTourMaps.map((map) => (
      <div class="wide-photo">
        <Image src={map.image} alt={map.alt} widths={[480, 900, 1600, 2000]} sizes="100vw" />
      </div>
    ))}
  </Section>

  <Section label="Book" heading="Choose your hike, then your day." id="reserver">
    <p>
      Three steps: the hike, the month, then the day. Each participant then sends their own booking. Nothing to pay at this stage: we receive your booking, then email you the payment link for your deposit.
    </p>
    <NoteBox>
      <p>
        Payment: after your booking, we email you the PayPal link for the 50% deposit; the remaining 50% is due before the hike starts. Cancellation: no refund within {amistadWildCrossing.noRefundDays} days of departure. A departure runs from {amistadWildCrossing.minPeople} registered participants.
      </p>
      <p>
        Each participant fills in their own form and pays their own deposit. At the start of the hike, each participant signs their form and the liability waiver.
      </p>
      <p>
        In case of extreme weather, if we have to cancel the outing: full refund, or postponement to the next departure day.
      </p>
      <p>
        Already a group of {amistadWildCrossing.maxPeople}? We can open another day for you. Write to us on{' '}
        <a href={business.whatsappHref}>WhatsApp at {business.phone}</a> or at{' '}
        <a href={`mailto:${business.email}`}>{business.email}</a>.
      </p>
    </NoteBox>
    <HikeBooking options={hikeOptions} locale="en" />
  </Section>

  <Section label="In the Field" heading="A forest best met on foot.">
    <PhotoGrid items={trailPhotos} groupId="hiking" variant="varied" />
  </Section>

  <Fragment slot="footer">
    <div class="section-label">Pair It With</div>
    <h2>Early mornings belong to the birds.</h2>
    <p>Many guests combine a dawn birdwatching walk with a longer hike later in the day.</p>
    <div class="contact-list">
      <a href="/birdwatching/">Birdwatching →</a>
      <a href="/farm/">Back to The Farm →</a>
    </div>
  </Fragment>
</PageLayout>
